n("p47-late-cell-floors","open-lemma","P47 late-cell WOL-C floors (cells 417-424)","Lambda < 0.145 by route P needs 125 missing P47 late-cell floors; cells 417-424 (0.88 sharp) need point bound + 0.008 and stalled at 0.10-0.19. Floors are suprema over the Kronecker torus with all prime phases free and carry no height coordinate.","conjectural","no","no",R("route-1-finish-route-p-2026-10-06"),["lambda","torus"],"F6")
n("barrier-floor-not-binding","obstruction","Lowered barrier floor moves no Lambda value","The barrier floor is not an input of route P; under Polymath15 Thm 1.2 it enters only through containment (t0 <= 129/800, f^2 <= y0^2), which does not bind. 0.1787854 and 0.1758354 are unchanged at every floor from 0.1809 to 0.022.","closed","no","no",R("route-2-lowered-barrier-floor-2026-10-06"),["lambda","heat-flow"])
n("lemma-mp3-multipoint-phase","identity","Lemma MP3 (multi-point phase lemma)","For omega_s >= 0, |z| = |u_s| = 1, eps = +-1, c_s >= c0 >= 0: sum omega_s c_s [1 - eps Re(z u_s)] >= c0 (sum omega_s - |sum omega_s u_s|), sharp in z. One pair without centre weight is Raymond's Lemma 3. Worth -7.86e-7 on Lambda.","proved","no","no",R("route-3-three-point-probes-2026-10-07"),["lambda","torus"])
n("probe-measure-linearity","mechanism","Linearity of the floor in the probe measure","Kernel inequality, self cap and the Lemma H2 far-field inequality are linear in the probe measure, so mixtures of certified components need no new kernel certificate (lambda = min of components). Six certified lambda<2 two-point kernels give -2.28e-4.","certified","no","no",R("route-3-three-point-probes-2026-10-07"),["lambda"])
n("fejer-riesz-branch-reduction","tool","Fejer-Riesz branch-reduction lemma for fibre maxima","The fibre function g_q (terms |sin k theta|, k <= 7, |sin theta/2|, max(h_s,0)) has sup equal to the max over 1024 sign/branch choices of a trigonometric polynomial of degree <= 14; whole-circle Fejer-Riesz certifies it with residual <= 1.05e-12. Gain equals grid Lipschitz slack only.","proved","no","no",R("route-4-fejer-riesz-wol-2026-10-07"),["lambda","torus"])
n("multiband-lemma-b","mechanism","Theorem B'_m: multi-band Lemma B with line walls","Band argument split into m bands by certified line walls and local RH windows (width > 7252): 4 bands give 0.145620383931826, band 1 binds. Slab walls instead of line walls cost about c f^4/8 in Lambda. Unrefereed.","certified","no","no",R("route-5-many-bands-2026-10-07"),["lambda","heat-flow"])
n("sparse-verification-theorem-n","mechanism","Theorems S and N: sparse RH verification in the Lemma-B framework","RH must be verified contiguously to a head x_*(tau); above it one local window wider than the far-field distance D_K = 921-1639 with right wall >= x_**(tau) replaces contiguous verification to x_**/2 (about 1.73e12 ordinate units at tau = 0.145). Framework-relative.","proved","no","no",R("route-6-sparse-verification-2026-10-07"),["lambda","zero-free"])
n("lemma-cg-lambda-euler-weights","identity","Lemma CG^lambda: weighted Euler mollifier head coefficients","The head coefficient of prod_{p in {2,3,5}} (1 - lambda_p b_t(p) p^{-s}) is a convex combination of Lemma CG covers with weights prod lambda_p prod (1 - lambda_p); so 0 <= c_n(t_L) <= c_n(t) <= c_n(t_R) for lambda_p in [0,1]. lambda = 1 is already optimal.","proved","yes","no",R("route-7-time-dependent-mollifiers-2026-10-08"),["mollifier","lambda","euler-product"])
n("polymath-raymond-hybrid-no-gain","obstruction","Polymath/Raymond hybrid gives no gain","Joining lemma B'_P: a hybrid's bound is the max over its bands, Lambda <= max(U_1..U_m, t0 + y0^2/2). Any Polymath band from existing rows gives 0.1758354, which is +0.030141 above route P; the best split has no Polymath band.","closed","no","no",R("route-8-polymath-raymond-hybrid-2026-10-08"),["lambda","heat-flow"])
n("barrier-height-schedule-w4","tool","Optimised barrier height set W4","A 10-knot piecewise-linear multiplier of Raymond's PLAN heights added to the multi-height menu gives 0.145637425999752 alone (-5.67e-5), and exactly 0 once the route-3 kernels are present. Local, not global, optimum.","certified","no","no",R("route-9-barrier-height-schedule-2026-10-08"),["lambda"])
n("lean-cg-covering-identity","tool","Lean: Lemma CG covering identity and G0-a","Lean 4 theorem: c_n(t) = sum_{d|(n,30)} mu(d) beta_d(t) b_t(n/d) satisfies 0 <= c_n(t') <= c_n(t) for n >= 1, 0 <= t' <= t, with no hypotheses. Covering identity over ordered half-edge atoms exp(t a_p a_q/4) - 1.","proved","yes","yes",R("route-10-lean-core-raymond-chain-2026-10-14"),["lean","mollifier","heat-flow"])
n("lean-halfplane-substitution","identity","Lean: zero-free half-plane to strip and Lambda","Lean theorem: zeta(s) != 0 for Re s > theta >= 1/2 implies every zero of H_t, t >= 0, has Im(z)^2 <= max((2 theta - 1)^2 - 2t, 0), and Lambda <= (2 theta - 1)^2/2. theta = 7/8 gives Lambda <= 9/32; theta = 1 gives 1/2 from Mathlib alone.","proved","no","yes",R("route-10-lean-core-raymond-chain-2026-10-14"),["lean","lambda","zero-free","heat-flow"],"F4")
# --- B group
n("multi-rung-weil-symbol","identity","Multi-rung Weil symbol w_K","For support 2a <= ln(K+1) the pole-free Weil form is W(h) = (1/2 pi) int w_K |h^|^2 with w_K = 2 theta' - sum_{n<=K} beta_n cos(t ln n), beta_n = 2 Lambda(n)/sqrt n; rungs n > K drop out, so a certificate at ln(K+1) covers every smaller support.","proved","no","yes",R("route-11-multi-prime-toeplitz-krein-2026-10-09"),["weil","explicit-formula","twin-ladder"])
n("arb-lege-margins-decay","measured-phenomenon","ARB-LEGE certified margins past ln 3","Pole-free Weil positivity W(h) >= c ||h||^2 certified at 2a <= ln 4 (c = 8.55e-8), ln 5 (2.25e-12), ln 6 (6.25e-17); margins decay like 10^(-4.8 e^{2a}). The whole range lies below the verified-height crossover 2a = 7.764.","certified","no","no",R("route-11-multi-prime-toeplitz-krein-2026-10-09"),["weil","pick","zero-free"],"P19")
n("virtual-rungs-positive-extension","mechanism","Virtual rungs: positive-extension freedom outside |u| < 2a","Adding cosines with frequencies |u_j| >= 2a (u = ln r, r rational, r >= K+1 or r <= 1/(K+1)) leaves W unchanged on support 2a; with the floor lemma w_K + f >= 2 theta'(T) - F for F >= sup_torus(P - f). Best floor is lambda_max of the rung operator (Krein extension).","proved","no","yes",R("route-11-multi-prime-toeplitz-krein-2026-10-09"),["weil","torus","de-branges"])
n("semilocal-s23-fourier","identity","Semilocal Fourier transform F_S for S = {inf, 2, 3}","F_S eta(w) = sum_{a,b>=-1} c_2(a) c_3(b) eta^(2^a 3^b w), c_p(k) = 1 - 1/p (k >= 0), -1/p (k = -1); Mellin multiplier rho_2 rho_3 with rho_p(s) = (1 - p^{s-1})/(1 - p^{-s}), unimodular on Re s = 1/2. For g-support < ln 4, W = L_S - D_S exactly. Conditional on Connes-Consani framework.","conjectural","yes","unknown",R("route-12-semilocal-s23-identity-2026-10-09"),["weil","trace-formula","euler-product"])
n("semilocal-remainder-share-tautology","obstruction","Remainder share D_S/L_S cannot separate prime sets","On the unit-norm W-minimiser, 1 - share = lambda_W/L_S(h0) by definition for any decomposition W = L_S - D_S; share is 99.71%-99.99997% on [ln 3, ln 4] for S = {inf,2}, {inf,2,3}, {inf,2,3,5} alike. A statement about the metric at cutoff 1, not about the S -> all primes limit.","closed","yes","no",R("route-12-semilocal-s23-identity-2026-10-09"),["weil","trace-formula"])
n("semilocal-trace-side-positivity","measured-phenomenon","Semilocal trace side positive and growing with S","Trace-side symbol L^_S(0): +0.0650 (S = {inf,2}), +0.0504 (S3), +0.10 to +0.12 (S = {inf,2,3}), positive on [0,30]; Galerkin lambda_min(L_S23) = 0.175-0.225, lambda_min(L_S235) = 0.22-0.26. Not a certificate; the limit S -> all primes with cutoff -> infinity was not tested.","measured","yes","unknown",R("route-12-semilocal-s23-identity-2026-10-09"),["weil","trace-formula","euler-product"])
n("lac-eq-caratheodory-interpolation","identity","LAC-EQ: lacunary Weil positivity as Caratheodory interpolation","Weil positivity on the cone spanned by e^{-nu t}, nu in Lambda, holds iff a Caratheodory function on Re w > 0 interpolates xi'/xi(1/2 + nu) on Lambda (Nevanlinna-Pick, Stieltjes in x = nu^2). For Blaschke Lambda (sum 1/nu < infinity) the problem is indeterminate.","proved","no","yes",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","weil","de-branges"],"P18")
n("lacunary-cone-4k-certificate","measured-phenomenon","Certified Pick margin on the cone {4^k}","Infinite normalised Pick operator of xi on Lambda_4 = {4^k}: M >= 3.6346e-4 I (Arb; head >= 6.12e-4 minus IMS localisation 2.4854e-4). Float margins: 3.89e-9 (2^k), 1.06e-21 (2^{k/2}). Insensitive to zeros above height 80 in a double-zero to quadruple model.","certified","no","no",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","weil"],"P18")
n("lacunary-detection-horizon-law","measured-phenomenon","Detection horizon of geometric lattices: T h about 7","On lattices 2^{k/m} the Pick operator detects a planted off-line zero only below heights 23.0, 31.7, 39.3, 60.1 (m = 2,3,4,6), T h about 7. Heuristic resolution law Delta(gamma) = 1/sum 2 nu/(nu^2 + gamma^2); reaching 3e12 geometrically needs h ~ 1e-11 and margins ~ e^{-pi^2/h}.","measured","no","no",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","weil"],"P18")
n("near-muntz-threshold-cones","open-lemma","Near-Muntz-threshold Blaschke cones nu_k = k^p","For non-separated Blaschke node sets nu_k = k^p, p = 1.1-1.25, the heuristic horizon T_p ~ (2.2 C_p)^{p/(p-1)} passes 3e12 near p = 1.13 while margins tend to 0. Whether such cones carry zero information above the verified height is open; reduction to the pointwise wall is an analogy.","conjectural","no","no",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","weil","zero-free"])
n("bounded-type-lemma-xi-logderiv","open-lemma","Bounded-type lemma for xi'/xi(1/2 + w)","'A complete discrete (Muntz-complete) node set forces the interpolant G = xi'/xi(1/2 + w), hence RH' is conditional on a bounded-type lemma for xi'/xi(1/2 + w) in Re w > 0; the written argument uses the identity theorem on the whole interval (1, infinity).","conjectural","no","yes",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","de-branges"])
n("lac-sens-displacement-bound","identity","LAC-SENS: sensitivity of Pick data to horizontal displacement","Moving a zero at ordinate gamma horizontally by delta changes the interpolation data by at most delta^2 sup|g_gamma''| <= 2.914 delta^2/gamma^3. Off-line displacement enters lacunary Pick data at second order with cubic height decay.","proved","no","no",R("route-13-lacunary-muntz-cones-2026-10-09"),["pick","zero-channel"])
n("family-weil-symbol","identity","Family-averaged Weil symbol over characters mod q","Average over the q-2 nonprincipal characters: sigma_F(t) = log(q/pi) + [(q-3) Re psi(1/4 + it/2) + (q-1) Re psi(3/4 + it/2)]/(2(q-2)) - sum beta_n cos(t log n), beta_n = 2 Lambda(n) n^{-1/2}((q-1)[n = 1 mod q] - 1)/(q-2). No pole terms.","proved","no","yes",R("route-14-family-weil-positivity-2026-10-09"),["weil","explicit-formula","large-sieve"])
n("family-positivity-euler-blind","obstruction","Family Weil positivity is Euler-blind","Family positivity is certified to 2a about 2 log q (10.0 at q = 257) through orthogonality plus the conductor term log q. A family containing the RH-false Davenport-Heilbronn function is certified positive at 2a = 7.764. At all supports it is GRH for every character mod q.","closed","no","no",R("route-14-family-weil-positivity-2026-10-09"),["weil","large-sieve","euler-product"],"P23")
n("certificate-type-limit-lemma","obstruction","Limit of symbol-floor certificates","For a certificate W >= c ||h||^2 built from a compact Galerkin part with cutoff T: c <= inf_{|t|>=T} sigma(t). A point sigma(t0) < 0 with t0 >= T rules out every such certificate with cutoff T <= t0. Individual characters reach only 2a about 1.95-2.40 by this method.","proved","no","no",R("route-14-family-weil-positivity-2026-10-09"),["weil","pick"])
n("epstein-twins-control","control","Epstein zeta twins, class number 2-4","27 Epstein zeta functions of binary quadratic forms (same gamma factor and conductor as zeta_K, no Euler product for non-trivial classes) are Arb-certified Weil-negative at support a* <= A; principal forms fail near log(|D|/4) - 0.13 (even sector, measured).","certified","no","no",R("route-15-epstein-euler-blindness-2026-10-09"),["weil","euler-product","theta","torus"])
n("odd-sector-pole-term","identity","Odd-sector pole term of the Weil form","For odd real test g the pole term becomes -2 (int g sinh(x/2))^2 <= 0 (even: +2 (int g cosh(x/2))^2), so the odd sector can fail first: D = -23 principal form goes negative at about 1.662 (odd) against (1.679, 1.689] (even).","proved","no","yes",R("route-15-epstein-euler-blindness-2026-10-09"),["weil","explicit-formula"])
# --- C group
n("af-rank-trace-inertia","mechanism","Alpoge-Furman mechanism: rank-trace inequality and Sylvester inertia","Proportion >= 2/3 comes from Montgomery's pair-correlation second moment, a rank-trace inequality (Lemma 3.2) and Sylvester inertia applied to a Gabor compression G of Weil's Hermitian form (phi(u) e^{i alpha_k u}, support L = log(T/2 pi)). Measured: tr G = N(T,2T) +- 1 for T = 1e3 to 2.9e5.","measured","yes","no",R("route-16-alpoge-furman-twin-ladder-2026-10-10"),["pair-correlation","weil","twin-ladder","explicit-formula"],"P27")
n("af-closed-form-constants","identity","Closed forms in the 2/3 argument","R(psi0) = 4/3; R(psi_MT) = 1/2 + cot(1/sqrt2)/sqrt2 = 1.32749929632, so 2 - R = 0.672500703679 (Lamzouri C0); R_lambda(psi0) = 1/lambda + lambda/3, H(lambda) = 2 - 1/lambda - lambda/3 increasing on (0,1]; Christoffel value Lambda_2(0) = 5/36, 1 - 2 Lambda_2(0) = 13/18.","proved","no","no",R("route-16-alpoge-furman-twin-ladder-2026-10-10"),["pair-correlation","weil"],"P27")
n("af-hl-star-hierarchy","conjecture","HL*(k) hierarchy gives proportion 13/18 and 100%","Statements of the Alpoge-Furman preprint (arithmetic reproduced only): under a Hardy-Littlewood-type hypothesis HL*(4) the proportion of zeros on the line is >= 13/18; HL*(k) for all k gives 100%. A proportion statement, not an every-window statement.","conjectural","yes","no",R("route-16-alpoge-furman-twin-ladder-2026-10-10"),["pair-correlation","weil","large-sieve"])
n("conrey-kappa-theta-table","measured-phenomenon","Conditional one-piece Conrey kappa(theta) table","Conditional on the twisted second moment at length theta: kappa passes 5/12 at theta = 0.58508, 1/2 at 0.75515, 2/3 at 1.31084, equals 0.5884 at theta = 1; d kappa/d theta = 0.5707 at 4/7. Finite-T recipe main term matches direct averages to theta = 2 within 0.52% (55 configurations).","measured","yes","no",R("route-17-mollifiers-beyond-four-sevenths-2026-10-10"),["mollifier","large-sieve"],"P26")
n("jensen-loss-in-levinson","measured-phenomenon","Jensen step loses most of the mollified signal","Finite-T kappa with / without the Jensen inequality: 0.4903 / 0.8578 at theta = 4/7, T = 1e6; 0.6587 / 0.9434 at theta = 1. Mollifier alone: mean |psi|^2 / diagonal in [0.992, 1.011].","measured","yes","no",R("route-17-mollifiers-beyond-four-sevenths-2026-10-10"),["mollifier"],"P26")
n("pair-statistic-insensitivity","obstruction","Insensitivity lemma: n-level statistics are beta-blind","A normalised pair or n-level statistic with fixed bounded compactly supported test changes by O(H (log T)^{c_n}/T) when zeros in windows of total length H are changed; so GUE + O(T^{-delta}) is consistent with moving zeros off the line in windows shorter than T^{1-delta}. Point-set statement only.","proved","no","no",R("route-18-local-levinson-pair-correlation-2026-10-10"),["pair-correlation","zero-channel"],"P31")
n("gue-palm-coalesced-pair","identity","GUE Palm density at a coalesced pair","GUE Palm density given a coalesced pair: rho(u) = 1 - S^2 - 3 S'^2/pi^2 (S the sine kernel), deficit integral exactly 2 (Parseval). Linearised zero-ODE mode rate (4/s^2)(pi theta/2 - theta^2/4). Mirror count 3.021 against required p_req = 4.3743.","proved","no","no",R("route-18-local-levinson-pair-correlation-2026-10-10"),["pair-correlation","heat-flow","zero-channel"])
n("mollified-weil-reduction","obstruction","Mollified Weil form reduces to the plain Weil form","With M(s) = sum_{n<=N} m_n n^{-s}, mu = sum m_n n^{-1/2} delta_{log n}, h = g*g~: sum_rho h^(gamma_rho) M(rho) M(1-rho) = W(G*G~), G = mu*g supported in [-a, a + log N]. So a*_mol >= a*_plain - (1/2) log N; DH passes whenever 2a + log N <= ln 11.","closed","no","no",R("route-19-mollified-weil-forms-2026-10-10"),["mollifier","weil","explicit-formula"])
n("mollifier-holomorphy-constraint","identity","Holomorphy constraint on mollifier weights","A weight with an explicit-formula representation equal to |M(1/2 + it)|^2 on the line weights off-line zeros by M(rho) M(1 - rho), not |M(rho)|^2. A finite-length weight Phi(rho) Phi*(1 - rho) with measure support L gives the plain form at A = a + L/2.","proved","no","yes",R("route-19-mollified-weil-forms-2026-10-10"),["mollifier","weil","zero-channel"])
# --- D group
n("explicit-kkl-threshold","tool","Explicit Ki-Kim-Lee threshold x0(t)","For t in [t_lo, 1/2] all zeros of H_t with Re z >= x0(t_lo) + 0.47 are real and simple, x0(t) about 4 pi exp(c/t), c = 5.31-5.76 on [0.1, 0.2] (Arb; conditional on Polymath15 Thm 1.3 and de Bruijn). At X = 6e12 it covers only t >= 0.217.","certified","no","no",R("route-20-effective-ki-kim-lee-2026-10-07"),["heat-flow","lambda"])
n("kkl-triangle-method-floor","obstruction","Triangle-method floor c > 4.9144 for KKL constants","Every term of D(1/2; t, L) is >= n^{-1/2 - tL/4} and sum_{n=2}^{690988} n^{-1.7286} = 1.0000095 > 1, so D(1/2) < 1 fails whenever t log(x0/4 pi) <= 4.9144 (asymptotically 4(s0 - 1/2), zeta(s0) = 2). Beating route P needs c <= 3.912.","closed","no","yes",R("route-50-kkl-lambda-curve-2026-10-08"),["heat-flow","lambda"])
n("zero-flow-graph-laplacian","identity","Heat-flow zero dynamics as a weighted graph Laplacian","For polynomial heat flows d_t f = -f'': dz/dt = L(z) conj(z), L the Laplacian of the zero graph with weights w_kj = 2/|z_k - z_j|^2; dx/dt = +Lx, dy/dt = -Ly. Conserved: sum z_k, sum x_k y_k; sum z_k^2 = sum z_k(0)^2 + 2n(n-1)t.","proved","no","yes",R("route-21-zero-flow-entropy-functionals-2026-10-11"),["heat-flow","zero-channel","vortex"])
n("zero-flow-majorization","obstruction","Majorization theorems for the zero flow are flow-blind","Theorem A: y(t2) is majorized by y(t1) for t1 < t2. Theorem A': sum F(x_k,y_k) is nonincreasing along every heat flow iff F_xx <= 0 <= F_yy. Theorem B: sum psi(|Im z_k|) nonincreasing when y psi'(y) is nondecreasing. All hold for polynomials with non-real zeros: forward-only soft inequalities.","closed","no","yes",R("route-21-zero-flow-entropy-functionals-2026-10-11"),["heat-flow","zero-channel","antibridge"],"F1")
n("de-bruijn-sharp-in-ymax","identity","de Bruijn bound sharp in y_max; count above a height not monotone","Lambda <= t0 + y_max(t0)^2/2 is sharp as a function of y_max alone (isolated pair z^2 + Y^2 becomes real at t = Y^2/2). The count of zeros above a fixed height is not monotone: {+-0.9i, 0.001 +- 1.3i} goes from 1 to 2 zeros above height 1 by t = 0.02.","proved","no","yes",R("route-21-zero-flow-entropy-functionals-2026-10-11"),["heat-flow","lambda","zero-channel"])
n("csv-lehmer-criterion","tool","Csordas-Smith-Varga Lehmer-pair criterion","With D = gamma_{k+1} - gamma_k and G = sum over other +-gamma_j of [(gamma_k - gamma_j)^{-2} + (gamma_{k+1} - gamma_j)^{-2}]: if D^2 G < 4/5 then Lambda >= ((1 - (5/4) D^2 G)^{4/5} - 1)/(2G). Best found over 1.55e6 zeros to 1e13: Lambda >= -4.2577e-6; superseded by Rodgers-Tao.","certified","no","no",R("route-22-lehmer-pair-hunt-2026-10-11"),["lambda","heat-flow","pair-correlation"],"P31")
n("cue-neff-small-gap-correction","measured-phenomenon","Finite-height small-gap deficit matches CUE_Neff","Pooled gaps s < 0.2 over 1.55e6 zeros near 1e10-1e13: 12834 observed against 13186 GUE (0.9733 +- 0.0088) and 12782 CUE_Neff (1.004 +- 0.009). Replicates Bogomolny-Bohigas-Leboeuf-Monastra. 6.2-6.6% of pairs satisfy D^2 G < 4/5; lambda tail exponent 1.38-1.62.","measured","unknown","no",R("route-22-lehmer-pair-hunt-2026-10-11"),["pair-correlation"],"P31")
n("zero-ode-ht","identity","Zero ODE of H_t in unfolded units","Convention d_t H = -H_zz, zeros at z = 2 gamma: dz_k/dt = 2 sum' [1/(z_k - z_j) + 1/(z_k + z_j)] + 1/z_k for simple zeros; with tau = t/Dz^2, Dz = 4 pi/log(gamma/2 pi), dx_k/d tau = 2 sum' 1/(x_k - x_j) up to density-gradient corrections.","proved","no","yes",R("route-23-ht-vs-dyson-bm-2026-10-11"),["heat-flow","zero-channel","vortex"])
n("dyson-loop-identity-defect","measured-phenomenon","Zeros miss the Dyson loop identity by an arithmetic term","For CUE_N, E[g D] = -1 exactly (beta = 2 Ward identity). Zeta zeros at T about 1e6: Q = -0.9414 +- 0.003-0.004; Q + 1 = c 12 Lambda_B/L^2 with c = 0.434 +- 0.008 over L in [7,12], Lambda_B = 1.57314; equivalent beta_eff about 2.13. Finite-tau runs unfinished.","measured","yes","no",R("route-23-ht-vs-dyson-bm-2026-10-11"),["pair-correlation","heat-flow","euler-product"],"P31")
n("poisson-smoothed-count-ceiling","obstruction","Local-count channel capped at L/4; triangle method below de Bruijn ceiling","S_t(x,eta) = -Im(H_t'/H_t)(x + i eta) is the Poisson(eta)-smoothed zero count, and any x-uniform lower bound q satisfies q <= L/4 + o(1). The Polymath15 triangle criterion at X controls arg H_t only above sqrt(1-2t) for t <= 0.137. Ideal B2 channel ceiling Lambda about 0.148.","closed","no","no",R("route-24-mean-field-local-counts-2026-10-11"),["heat-flow","lambda","zero-channel"])
# --- E group
n("modular-scattering-factorisation","identity","Modular-surface scattering matrix through the bridge","phi(s) = Lambda(2s-1)/Lambda(2s) = c_inf(s) chi(2s-1) Z(s), c_inf = sqrt(pi) Gamma(s-1/2)/Gamma(s), chi the bridge, Z(s) = zeta(2-2s)/zeta(2s); equivalently phi = beta Z with beta = pi^{2s-1} Gamma(1-s)/Gamma(s), each unimodular on Re s = 1/2. Poles in 0 < Re s < 1/2 are exactly rho/2.","proved","no","yes",R("route-25-bridge-as-scattering-2026-10-12"),["bridge","trace-formula","twin-ladder"])
n("lax-phillips-axioms-rh-blind","obstruction","Scattering axioms survive moved resonances","Under xi -> xi Q_delta/Q_0 (an on-line pair replaced by an off-line quartet) phi_delta stays unitary on the axis, satisfies phi(s) phi(1-s) = 1, has positive residue at s = 1 and S = phi(s)(s-1)/s stays inner. The de Bruijn-flow phi_t keeps these for every real t.","closed","no","yes",R("route-25-bridge-as-scattering-2026-10-12"),["bridge","antibridge","trace-formula","heat-flow"],"G6")
n("scattering-causality-at-one-line","identity","Causality criterion sits at the zeta(1+it) level","The mirror resonance of a zero z = x + iy of H_t has Re s >= 1/2 iff |y| >= 1 iff Re w >= 1. The local all-pass factors z_p(s) = zeta_p(2-2s)/zeta_p(2s) need Re s > 1/2 and Re s < 1/2 at once: their product converges absolutely nowhere.","proved","yes","yes",R("route-25-bridge-as-scattering-2026-10-12"),["bridge","euler-product","trace-formula"],"G10")
n("scattering-winding-split","identity","Winding split of the scattering phase","W(T) = W_inf(T) + arg zeta(1 + 2iT)/pi + 1/2, with W_inf(T) ~ (T/pi) log(T/(pi e)). On the axis s = 1/2 + it the bridge is sampled at w = 2it: |chi(2it)| = sqrt(t/pi) sqrt(tanh pi t), cancelled exactly by |c_inf|.","proved","yes","yes",R("route-25-bridge-as-scattering-2026-10-12"),["bridge","trace-formula"])
n("gl2-weil-symbol","identity","Weil symbol of a holomorphic newform","For weight k, level N, trivial character: W(h) = (1/2 pi) int sigma |h^|^2, sigma(t) = log N - 2 log 2 pi + 2 Re psi(k/2 + it) - sum_{log n < 2a} 2 c(n) n^{-1/2} cos(t log n); no pole terms; N enters only as + log N ||h||^2.","proved","no","yes",R("route-26-gl2-twin-ladder-2026-10-12"),["weil","hecke","twin-ladder","explicit-formula"])
n("gl2-ramanujan-box-vertex","mechanism","Worst case over the Ramanujan box is a vertex","lambda_min of the Weil form is concave in the rung amplitudes, so over |lambda_f(p)| <= 2 the worst case is a vertex (lambda(p) = +2). If c0(k,N) = log N - 2 log 2 pi + 2 psi(k/2) > sum_{n<e^{2a}} 4 Lambda(n)/sqrt n then W >= 0; holds for every weight >= 36 at 2a <= log 3.","proved","no","no",R("route-26-gl2-twin-ladder-2026-10-12"),["hecke","weil","twin-ladder"],"L3")
n("gl2-ramanujan-is-rung-rh","obstruction","Ramanujan is RH per rung, not for the ladder","For p not dividing N the 11a rung is 1/P_1(p^{-s}) with P_1 the H^1 factor of Z(E_p,T) (Hasse = curve RH); for weight k > 2 the rung lies in H^{k-1} of the Kuga-Sato variety (Deligne). Provable ladder statements are conductor-driven and Euler-blind (weight-24 non-eigenform also certified).","closed","yes","no",R("route-26-gl2-twin-ladder-2026-10-12"),["hecke","function-field","hodge","twin-ladder"],"L1")
n("ff-weil-form-intersection-identity","identity","Function-field twin-ladder Weil form = minus intersection form","On C x C over F_q with Frobenius graphs Gamma_j and P_j = Gamma_j - H - q^j V: q^j + q^k - Gamma_j.Gamma_k = -P_j.P_k = q^{(j+k)/2} S_{k-j}, S_n = q^{-n/2} sum alpha_i^n. Hodge index on span{P_j} gives Q_TL >= 0, hence RH for the curve.","proved","yes","yes",R("route-27-function-field-twin-ladder-2026-10-06"),["function-field","hodge","twin-ladder","weil"])
n("ff-ghost-index-toeplitz","identity","Exact ghost index of the Frobenius Toeplitz matrix","For N >= number of distinct Frobenius eigenvalues, T_N = [S_{j-k}] has exactly nu negative eigenvalues, nu = number of off-circle pairs; curve-RH iff T_{2g} >= 0. R_a(z) = X(q^a z)/X(q^{-a} z) is a degree-2g Blaschke product under RH. Sensitivity lambda_min(T_2g) = -C eps^2 + o(eps^2).","proved","no","yes",R("route-27-function-field-twin-ladder-2026-10-06"),["function-field","pick","twin-ladder"],"Q6")
n("ff-euler-product-fakes","control","Function-field fakes: Euler product without RH","215 exact polynomials in the census boxes (17 at q = 3, g = 2; 198 at q = 5, g = 2; g = 1: 1 - 5T + 5T^2, 1 + 6T + 7T^2) have an Euler product with nonnegative integer closed-point counts, functional equation, lossless bridge and rationality, with RH false. Lambda_C of fakes: +0.020 to +0.172.","certified","yes","yes",R("route-27-function-field-twin-ladder-2026-10-06"),["function-field","euler-product","twin-ladder"],"T3")
n("spec-z-squared-hodge-index","open-lemma","Missing surface Spec Z x Spec Z with a Hodge index theorem","The function-field proof lifts to Q only given (O3) a surface playing C x C with a Hodge index theorem on Frobenius-graph classes, and (O1) a regularisation of the infinite zero count (archimedean term as regularised self-intersection). Faltings-Hriljac covers fibred arithmetic surfaces, not the analogue of C x C.","conjectural","yes","yes",R("route-27-function-field-twin-ladder-2026-10-06"),["function-field","hodge","weil"],"T3")
n("ff-lambda-of-elliptic-curve","identity","de Bruijn-Newman analogue for elliptic curves over F_q","Lambda_E = 4 log(|a|/(2 sqrt q))/(log q)^2 (minus infinity at a = 0); sup over E/F_p tends to 0 along all primes with |sup Lambda_E| <= 4/((2 sqrt p - 1)(log p)^2); 0 exactly for maximal curves over F_{p^2}.","proved","no","yes",R("route-27-function-field-twin-ladder-2026-10-06"),["function-field","lambda","heat-flow"])
n("selberg-theorem-u-geodesic-monoid","identity","Theorem U on the geodesic monoid","For a finite set G of primitive geodesic classes the sieve algebra is span{T_D : D subset G}, dimension 2^|G|; every freeze word followed by a linear functional is L(diag(m) c) for a unique m. Telescope and five-shell identities are telescoping algebra with no zero information. Collapse: 72 instead of 256 for the first 8 classes.","proved","yes","no",R("route-28-selberg-zeta-freeze-sandbox-2026-10-12"),["trace-formula","euler-product","twin-ladder"])
n("selberg-phase-gate-vs-zeta","measured-phenomenon","Phase gate on sigma = 0.55: Selberg zeta against zeta","On sigma = 0.55, t <= 26, Re Z < 0 on 6.1% of the grid for the PSL2(Z) Selberg zeta against 0% for zeta (min Re zeta = 0.014); modulus-first threshold sigma*(0): zeta 1.578, Selberg 1.173. Attribution confounded by the rho/2 zero family at Re s = 1/4.","measured","yes","no",R("route-28-selberg-zeta-freeze-sandbox-2026-10-12"),["trace-formula","euler-product"])
n("selberg-control-pair","open-lemma","RH-true / RH-false Selberg control pair","No RH-false control was run in the Selberg sandbox. A pair (cocompact arithmetic group with the half-plane RH-analogue, against a group with an exceptional eigenvalue) would test whether Euler-product calculi over prime geodesics see zero location. Z = det(1 - L_s^2) (Mayer) supplies a transfer operator.","conjectural","yes","unknown",R("route-28-selberg-zeta-freeze-sandbox-2026-10-12"),["trace-formula","euler-product"])
n("interferometer-visibility-gauge","obstruction","Interferometer visibility is vacuous, false or a gauge choice","Split Lambda_F = A(s) + A(1-s), V = 2|A(s)||A(1-s)|/(|A(s)|^2 + |A(1-s)|^2). Exact arms give V0 = sech(log|chi|), a function of the gamma factor alone. A -> A + O with O(1-s) = -O(s) changes V; the bound sup V < 1 is certified false (79 crossings for zeta, t <= 200).","closed","no","no",R("route-29-interferometer-visibility-2026-10-12"),["bridge","twin-ladder","visualization"])
n("xi-arm-split-incomplete-gamma","identity","Arm split of the completed zeta function at the self-dual point","Lambda(s) = A(s) + A(1-s), A(s) = -1/s + sum_n (pi n^2)^{-s/2} Gamma(s/2, pi n^2). A(s) = -theta3(e^{-pi})/s + 4 psi'(1)/(s(s+2)) + O(t^{-3}), theta3(e^{-pi}) = pi^{1/4}/Gamma(3/4): each arm is ~1/t while Lambda ~ e^{-pi t/4}.","proved","no","yes",R("route-29-interferometer-visibility-2026-10-12"),["bridge","theta","twin-ladder"])
n("dh-partial-euler-factorisation","identity","Davenport-Heilbronn = partial Euler product times G","a(n mod 5) = (0, 1, kappa, -kappa, -1), kappa = 0.2840790438; a(nm) = a(n) a(m) for m = +-1 mod 5, so F_DH = [Euler product over p = +-1 mod 5] x G(s), G supported on integers built from primes = +-2 mod 5. Log-derivative coefficients c(n) vanish on 1031 non-prime-powers <= 3000, 906 nonzero.","proved","yes","yes",R("route-30-finite-support-euler-detector-2026-10-12"),["euler-product","twin-ladder"])
n("rung-toeplitz-euler-detector","mechanism","Rung Toeplitz (Herglotz) test detects DH at ln 2 / ln 4 / ln 6","Rung moments m_k(p) = c(p^k)/log p; for unitary local degree 1 the Toeplitz T_p^(K) = [m_|i-j|] is PSD. DH fails: lambda_min(T_2^(2)) = -1.15558, Szego limit -1.79360. Onsets sharp against formal local Euler products: ln 2 (unitary, full), ln 4 (even data), ln 6 (Euler only). No zero-location content.","certified","yes","no",R("route-30-finite-support-euler-detector-2026-10-12"),["euler-product","pick","twin-ladder","hecke"],"L1")
n("euler-detection-decouples-from-offline","measured-phenomenon","Rung data are read from the on-line zeros","From DH's zeros below 130 (71 on-line, 2 off-line pairs): c(2) = 0.1969085883 recovered at support 1.093 (error 3.2e-12), c(4) = -1.4422324 at 1.606; both off-line pairs together contribute 7e-7 / 1.7e-4. At small support Euler detection and off-line-zero detection decouple.","measured","yes","no",R("route-30-finite-support-euler-detector-2026-10-12"),["euler-product","explicit-formula","zero-channel"])
n("euler-aware-weil-radius","obstruction","Euler-aware Weil radius over unitary rung data","Proposed SDP: Weil positivity over the formal unitary degree-1 rung class, against the archimedean radius 0.9385 and DH's 1.72. The 2026-11 campaign measured class-uniform positivity over tempered local data only to support 0.7228 at conductor 1 (worst case alpha_2 = -1).","closed","yes","no",R("route-30-finite-support-euler-detector-2026-10-12"),["euler-product","weil","hecke"],"L3")
n("information-floor-ln2","obstruction","Information floor at support ln 2","For 2a <= ln 2 the prime side of the explicit formula is empty, so a twin and its Euler arm have the same Weil form and no quantity separates them. At conductor 1 there is no DH-type twin with zeta's bridge (Hamburger).","proved","no","yes",R("route-30-finite-support-euler-detector-2026-10-12"),["weil","explicit-formula","euler-product"])
