n("mv-cap-zero-side-theorem","obstruction","MV-CAP theorem for zero-side premises","Window replacement: for any centre c0 in [3.1e12, 7.50e16] a model zeta_W has a nonreal zero z* = 2c + 0.17i with mirror count <= 3.0119 < p_req = 4.3743, N(sigma,T) up by <= 1, new pair beta <= 0.585. A certifying zero-side premise needs slack < 19.3 zeros, relative precision <= 1.5e-12.","closed","no","no",R("route-42-formal-mv-cap-2026-10-10"),["zero-channel","large-sieve","antibridge"],"P29")
n("window-replacement-control","control","Window-replacement model xi_W","xi_W = kappa xi Q_{W'}/Q_W replaces the zeros in one window by a configuration with an off-line pair, keeping order 1, functional equation, reality and xi_W(1) = xi(1). The unshifted model fails O-form function-side premises (mean square moves by |kappa^2 - 1| T log T); the kappa = 1 shifted variant satisfies them.","proved","no","no",R("route-42-formal-mv-cap-2026-10-10"),["zero-channel","antibridge"],"P29")
