n("flow-criticality-grade-kappa","object","Graded flow-criticality kappa(P) = sup Lambda","kappa(P) = sup{Lambda(F) : F in P} over the de Bruijn class. kappa(Strip_Y) = Y^2/2 without Phi > 0: critical strip 1/2, QRH 7/8 gives 9/32, QRH 11/12 gives 25/72. Proportion, zero-density and 'all but finitely many on the line' add no kappa beyond their strip.","proved","no","yes",R("route-43-flow-criticality-classes-2026-10-14"),["heat-flow","lambda","zero-free","lean"])
n("exact-witness-quadratic-cosine","identity","Exact de Bruijn-Newman constant of (z^2 + Y^2) cos(cz)","Lambda((z^2 + Y^2) cos(cz)) = (sqrt(1 + 4 c^2 Y^2) - 1)/(4 c^2), tending to Y^2/2 as c -> 0. For c >= T the fixed-support Weil form satisfies W_T >= 0 iff 2c >= sinh(2YT)/Y - 2T; lower ladder T^2 kappa_low -> 0.349.","proved","no","yes",R("route-43-flow-criticality-classes-2026-10-14"),["heat-flow","lambda","weil"])
n("escape-law-backward-flow","obstruction","Escape law for the backward flow","Route 43 left open whether zeros of H_{-tau} leave every strip for every tau > 0 (measured: H_{-1} zero at 5040.39 + 1.41i; heuristic reach tau log(x/4 pi)/2 - 1). The 2026-11 campaign proved it (internal): every horizontal-strip statement true for xi is flow-critical; holds for DH.","closed","no","yes",R("route-43-flow-criticality-classes-2026-10-14"),["heat-flow","zero-free","antibridge"],"F1")
n("dirichlet-dh-twins-control","control","440 Dirichlet DH-type twins, conductors 5-49","For each conjugate pair of primitive characters mod q: F_theta = sum Re(e^{i theta} chi(n)) n^{-s}, e^{2i theta} = omega conj(eps(chi)), omega = +-1; same gamma factor and functional equation, no Euler product. q = 5, T+ is Davenport-Heilbronn. 387 certified Weil-negative at a in [0.36, 3.40]; 53 blind to a = 3.6.","certified","no","no",R("route-44-euler-detection-depth-2026-10-15"),["euler-product","weil"])
n("weil-sector-split","identity","Even/odd sector split of the Weil form","For real g = g_e + g_o the cross-correlations cancel in G(x) = int g(y) g(y+x) dy, so W(g) = W(g_e) + W(g_o) for every linear functional of G. A real zero beta in (1/2,1) contributes -(int g sinh((beta-1/2)x))^2 in the odd sector and +(int g cosh)^2 in the even.","proved","no","yes",R("route-44-euler-detection-depth-2026-10-15"),["weil","explicit-formula"])
n("weil-onset-zero-side-law","measured-phenomenon","Weil-negativity onset follows the first off-line zero","Fitted over 240 twins: a* = -0.748 + 0.387 log gamma - 0.278 log(beta - 1/2) + 0.278 log q (rms 0.139, R^2 0.883; predicts DH 1.746). Onset is set mainly by root-number phase; conductor slope 0.2-0.37 per log q against slope 1 for Epstein principal forms. Euler arms never negative.","measured","no","no",R("route-44-euler-detection-depth-2026-10-15"),["weil","zero-channel","euler-product"])
# --- J group
n("l-damped-finite-window-floor","open-lemma","Deterministic finite-window source floor at t > 0","For t > 0 the source at height x uses L = log(x/4 pi) and head amplitudes exp(t v(v - L)/4) damp as x grows, so uniformity in x forces a sup only over a finite x-window per L-band (x in [X-2, about 1.105X]). Realised heights sit 0.05-0.10 below the torus lower bound (heuristic).","conjectural","no","no",R("route-45-multiplicative-chaos-source-tails-2026-10-15"),["lambda","torus","heat-flow"],"F5")
n("source-field-finite-variance","measured-phenomenon","Source field is finite-variance Bohr-Jessen, not log-correlated","At the binding cells sigma_eff = (1+h)/2 in [0.88, 1.59]; labels <= 10 carry 93-98% of first-order variance. Steinhaus Monte Carlo: sd 0.099-0.115, Kronecker lower bounds 3.7-5.1 sd above the mean, lighter-than-Gaussian tails. Multiplicative-chaos maximum asymptotics do not apply.","measured","yes","no",R("route-45-multiplicative-chaos-source-tails-2026-10-15"),["torus","lambda"])
n("kronecker-sup-lower-bounds","measured-phenomenon","Certified Kronecker suprema at the 12 binding cells","Arb lower bounds on sup over the prime-phase torus of the leading-order source (labels <= 690988): >= 0.533514111339326 at t = 0.075. Any floor improvement is capped at U2 = 0.144254643222956; box growth 3-7x per added prime, k >= 6 primes out of reach.","certified","yes","no",R("route-46-exact-kronecker-floors-2026-10-06"),["torus","lambda"])
n("one-line-ambiguity-group","obstruction","Hilbert-transform wall: |xi| on the line fixes xi only up to off-line flips","G entire of order <= 1 with |G| = |xi| on Re s = 1/2 implies G = e^{i alpha + lambda(s - 1/2)} xi prod_{rho in S} B~_rho(s)/B~_rho(1/2), S any multiset of off-line zeros; each off-line quadruple has 9 configurations with identical modulus on the line.","closed","no","yes",R("route-48-phase-retrieval-zeta-2026-10-15"),["antibridge","zero-channel","bridge"])
n("fe-plus-reality-rigidity","identity","One line + functional equation + reality gives +-xi","If |G| = |xi| on the line and G* = G (G*(s) = conj G(1 - conj s)) then G^2 = xi^2, G = +-xi. Either symmetry alone fails: xi B~_rho B~_{1-rho} keeps FE without reality, xi B~_rho B~_{conj rho} keeps reality without FE.","proved","no","yes",R("route-48-phase-retrieval-zeta-2026-10-15"),["bridge","zero-channel"])
n("two-line-zero-detector","mechanism","Two-line zero detector D(w) (Poisson-Jensen)","For F = zeta(s)(s-1)/s: D(w) = log|F(w)| - P_w[log|F(1/2 + i.)|] = sum_{beta > 1/2} log|B_rho(w)| <= 0 on Re w > 1/2. Evaluated on Re w = sigma1 >= 1 it determines all zeros with beta > 1/2; found 8 DH off-line zeros below 400 (sigma1 > 1.39514 for DH).","proved","unknown","yes",R("route-48-phase-retrieval-zeta-2026-10-15"),["zero-channel","bridge","euler-product"])
n("bsy-interior-value-criterion","identity","One line + one interior value (Balazard-Saias-Yor extension)","J(a) = log|F(a)| deficit = sum_{beta > 1/2} -log|B_rho(a)| >= 0, equal to 0 iff no zeros right of the line; at a = 1 it is exactly Balazard-Saias-Yor. Decides RH but cannot locate zeros: an off-line quadruple contributes about 2 delta/gamma^2.","proved","unknown","no",R("route-48-phase-retrieval-zeta-2026-10-15"),["zero-channel","bridge"])
n("minimum-phase-hilbert-identity","identity","Minimum-phase identity on vertical lines","For 1/2 <= sigma < 1, F_sigma = zeta(s)(s-1)/(s + 1 - 2 sigma): arg F_sigma(sigma + it) = H_sigma[log|zeta(sigma + i.)|](t) + arg B_sigma(sigma + it), B_sigma the Blaschke product over zeros with beta > sigma; exact Hilbert relation iff no zeros right of sigma (sigma = 1/2: RH).","proved","no","yes",R("route-48-phase-retrieval-zeta-2026-10-15"),["zero-channel","bridge","antibridge"])
n("sawtooth-s-of-t-lemma","tool","Sawtooth lemma for S(T)","If |S_1(t2) - S_1(t1)| <= A(t2) and rho = theta'/pi, then S(t) <= A(t+delta)/delta + delta rho(t+delta)/2 and S(t) >= -A(t)/delta - delta rho(t)/2; optimal delta gives |S(t)| <= sqrt(2 A rho)(1+o(1)): 5.6748 against 6.6612 at 3e12. Input constant (Trudgian 2011) unchecked.","proved","no","yes",R("route-49-unconditional-s-of-t-2026-10-06"),["zero-channel","explicit-formula"])
n("s-of-t-channel-no-lever","obstruction","Pointwise S(T) bounds give no Lambda lever","Counting-input ceiling for mirror descent p_E(Y) = 4 rho_z (pi/2 - arctan((E+1)/(rho_z Y))): the all-real model needs E <= 3.363 for formal Lambda 0.2 while the proved E = 5.675 gives 0.2424. Beurling-Selberg extremal functions do not help: off-line zeros in short windows lack local density control.","closed","no","no",R("route-49-unconditional-s-of-t-2026-10-06"),["lambda","zero-channel","large-sieve"])
TYPES={"object","mechanism","identity","measured-phenomenon","open-lemma","obstruction","control","tool","conjecture"}
ST={"proved","certified","measured","conjectural","refuted","closed"}
ids=set(); bad=0
